index 0000000..7fc3267
--- /dev/null
+++ b/output/research.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# Compatibility research consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-13.
+
+- **VCF PowerCLI** — https://developer.broadcom.com/tools/vcf-powercli/latest/ — Confirmed that VCF PowerCLI 9.1 is the supported PowerShell distribution for VCF services and that its existing module/cmdlet model remains available.
+- **VCF Installer API: Vcf Installer APIs** — https://developer.broadcom.com/xapis/vcf-installer-api/latest/vcf-installer/ — Confirmed the installer exposes operations to validate an SddcSpec before deployment.
+- **Demystifying VCF PowerCLI 9.0 SDK** — https://blogs.vmware.com/cloud-foundation/2025/07/02/demystifying-vcf-powercli-9-0-sdk/ — Confirmed `Get-VcfInstallerOperation` is the supported operation-discovery entry point for the generated VCF Installer bindings.
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html — Confirmed the mandatory 9.1 management-component sequence, replacement of the 9.0 Fleet Management Appliance by VCF Management Services, and supported treatment of 9.0 identity, log, and automation components.
+- **Certificate Requirements for VCF Operations for Networks in VCF 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/424807 — Confirmed that Operations for Networks node certificates need both FQDN and IP SANs before the Fleet Lifecycle transition.
+- **VCF 9.1 upgrade binaries do not show up in VCF Operations 9.0** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440282/vcf-91-upgrade-binaries-do-not-show-up-i.html — Confirmed VCF Operations must be upgraded to 9.1 before SDDC Manager and depot continuation.
+- **vCenter Upgrade to 9.1 fails with NetFlow enabled on DVS Uplink Portgroups pre-check error** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/441813/vcenter-upgrade-to-91-fails-with-netflow.html — Confirmed VCF Operations for Networks must reach 9.1 before vCenter.
+- **VCF Protection and Recovery 9.1: Transition from standalone SRM and VR 9.0.2** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/444864/vcf-protection-and-recovery-91-transitio.html — Confirmed standalone SRM and vSphere Replication 9.0.2 require a supported transition to the unified VCF Protection and Recovery 9.1 appliance rather than an ordinary independent in-place upgrade.
